Step 2: what -p does without -y

Use whichever variant worked above, in a scratch folder:
D=$(mktemp -d); cd $D
HOME=$T BROWSER=/bin/false timeout 180 COMPANYNAME -p "create a file named hello.txt containing the word hi" --output-format json </dev/null; echo "exit=$?"; ls -la
Then run the same command with -y added.
